    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "41a62c75_21367c27",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-02T18:12:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could you give an example of a module that is `installable: false` and a dependency of the microdroid/cuttlefish system image? I\u0027m trying to understand why we can\u0027t just make `installable: false` act the same as `no_full_install: true`.",
      "revId": "3f627e661a272b6f5b231880815e90f11a60ffe2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5d9f6c9_a1f4b59b",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-02T22:06:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure. Please see the modules that are touched by the submitted-together changes. `apexd.microdroid` is a good example. Both `apexd` and `apexd.microdroid` are installed to `/system/bin/apex`. https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/q/topic:%22hide_from_make%22\n\nre: make `installable: false` act the same as `no_full_install: true`\n\nThe problem of `installable` is that it\u0027s not available to every module (i.e. `android.Module`). I could go in that direction, but that would be been a much more intrusive change; I didn\u0027t like that. Another reason was that the expression `installable: false` is misleading because we still do install the module to filesystem modules.\n\nI think, in the long term, we should deprecate `no_full_install` (while keeping `installable`) if we stop making filesystem image in Make.",
      "parentUuid": "41a62c75_21367c27",
      "revId": "3f627e661a272b6f5b231880815e90f11a60ffe2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dda2882d_b8dde351",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-02T22:36:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think moving it to `android.Module` is a big deal. Creating a separate property that does something very similar is more tech debt than an \"intrusive change\" IMO.\n\n\u003e I think, in the long term, we should deprecate no_full_install (while keeping installable) if we stop making filesystem image in Make.\n\nIn the long term, I think we should deprecate both of these properties. If you want something to not be installed, you just wouldn\u0027t list it as a dependency of the filesystem image.",
      "parentUuid": "c5d9f6c9_a1f4b59b",
      "revId": "3f627e661a272b6f5b231880815e90f11a60ffe2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0dfb5378_25c3c69f",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-02T23:00:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There can be build-only dependencies like stubs. You don\u0027t want to install it even if there\u0027s a dependency to it from a filesystem module (or listed in PRODUCT_PACKAGES).\n\nI think that\u0027s where `installable: false` will still be necessary.\n\nIf you agree on that `installable` shall persist AND we will be deprecating placing files to \"out/target/product\", I think it\u0027s better to introduce a new property that only handles that aspect only. Otherwise we will have to distinguish two different meanings of `installable: false`: (1) don\u0027t install this anywhere, (2) just don\u0027t put it to out/target/product.",
      "parentUuid": "dda2882d_b8dde351",
      "revId": "3f627e661a272b6f5b231880815e90f11a60ffe2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "498249f7_c3265e98",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-02T23:03:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well stubs will never be installed, so they won\u0027t emit any packaging specs in the first place. So I don\u0027t think they\u0027re a valid reason to keep `installable: false`.",
      "parentUuid": "0dfb5378_25c3c69f",
      "revId": "3f627e661a272b6f5b231880815e90f11a60ffe2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7243f736_c8dbf6f5",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-02T23:11:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There could be a hand-crafted stubs which is just seen as a normal cc_library to Soong. I remember we have such in AOSP as well, but forgot what it was.\n\nThere are many more build-only artifacts. Just see https://cs.android.com/search?q\u003df:%5C.bp%20installable:%5C%20false%20-f:test\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain\u0026start\u003d31",
      "parentUuid": "498249f7_c3265e98",
      "revId": "3f627e661a272b6f5b231880815e90f11a60ffe2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
